# STUDENT SLIDESHOW FORGE — Creativity Techniques (UEM)

Every forged **lesson** ships a short Reveal.js slideshow, visually consistent
with [How to Pass Creativity Techniques](/tracks/ct/how-to-pass-this-track/)
and with the sibling Digital Creativity student decks
(`digital-creativity-uem` · `STUDENT-SLIDESHOW-FORGE.mdc` + `student-media-deck.js`).

**Binding parallel contract:** [`SESSION-RHYTHM-AND-DELIVERABLES.mdc`](./SESSION-RHYTHM-AND-DELIVERABLES.mdc)
(Masterclass → Lab/Portfolio → Workshop/Deliverable; D1–D5; geometrical BG law).

The slideshow is **not** the lesson text, not the professor research brief, and
not a research ledger. It is the in-class conceptual surface.

## Two surfaces per unit (do not collapse)

| Surface | Audience | Path pattern | Content |
| ------- | -------- | ------------ | ------- |
| **Professor brief** | Instructor | `creativity-techniques-pedagogy/forge/unit-enrichment/U*/PROFESSOR.md` (unpublished) | Full findings + session notes |
| **Student slideshow** | Cohort | `docs/tracks/en/uem/2627-ct/u-N-*/` + `data/content.json` | Ideas + Lab/Workshop framing; public-safe only |
| **Student lesson page** | Cohort | `docs/lessons/en/creativity-techniques/u-N-*/` | B1/B2/B3 prose; Chicago cites; gated provenance |

## Mandatory deck spine (programmatic)

Order is binding. Main Masterclass ideas stay **≤ 6**; Analysis / Lab / Workshop
frame slides are structural and do **not** count against that six.

```text
C  unit_cover                       background_kind: profield     ← REQUIRED FIRST
A  analysis_opener                  background_kind: geometrical   ← REQUIRED
A+ analysis_model (optional)        background_kind: profield
1… Masterclass ideas (≤ 6)          background_kind: profield | diagram
N  lab_opener                       background_kind: geometrical   ← REQUIRED
N+1…N+2  Exactly two Lab exercises (portfolio_bound)  background_kind: profield | none
M  workshop_opener                  background_kind: geometrical   ← from session 4 only
M+ Workshop work prompt             background_kind: none | diagram | profield
Z  outro / carry-forward            background_kind: geometrical   ← REQUIRED
```

**Lab exercise count (binding):** **exactly two** `lab_exercise` slides per ordinary unit — concentrate meaning into those two; do not forge three or more. Lesson B2 must match. If a selection rubric is needed, make it a phase inside Exercise 2 rather than a third slide.

**First lessons (sessions 1–3):** omit `workshop_opener` / `workshop_work` entirely — session ends after Lab. Do not invent side deliverables. **D1 Analysis** never receives Workshop clock. **From session 4:** Workshop ≈½ **D2 Transposition** · ≈½ **D3 final event**.

`unit_cover` is the unit title / stake slide. It comes **before** analysis. Do not open the deck on analysis alone.

`lab_opener` sentence (fixed intent, wording may vary slightly):

> Two exercises come next. Everything you produce in Lab goes into your **portfolio index**.

The student **lesson** must contain the Analysis method in prose (language / medium / support + when defences start). Do not leave analysis only on the deck.
## Background law

| Role | Background |
| ---- | ---------- |
| Analysis model · Masterclass · Lab exercises | Accepted **Profield** media (public-safe fields only) |
| Stance slides without a pack image | Course **diagram** — Koch triangle (`ct-koch-triangle-*.svg`), **not** Sierpinski |
| `analysis_opener` · `lab_opener` · `workshop_opener` · `outro` | **Geometrical only** (`fractal-pass-track` SVGs) |
| Never | Invented rights; Resource UUID / forger version in captions; Sierpinski as Masterclass fallback |
| Never | Non-geometrical decorative fallbacks on transition slides; geometrical captions must include the SVG content-hash UUID |

Typed fields on each slide object:

```yaml
slide_role: unit_cover | analysis_opener | analysis_model | masterclass | lab_opener | lab_exercise | workshop_opener | workshop_work | outro
background_kind: profield | geometrical | diagram | none
media_slot_id: U1.still.example   # when background_kind: profield
portfolio_bound: true | false
portfolio_trace: "Save … in the portfolio index."
quote: "Optional brief quotation (≤ ~40 words) — Ahmes-verbatim or Tao invent (see golden rule 3)."
quote_origin: page_verified | tao_invented   # required whenever quote is set; never put the corpus product name in student content.json
semantic_tags: []   # DH metadata for the quote — see golden rule 3
ttod_index:         # required for Tao invents; data-only, not rendered by default
  id: C-U2-example-01
  number: III
  form: Haiku
  fields: [fluencyFlexibilityOriginality, divergentThinking]
```

Student wording: prefer clear late-secondary / first-year voice. Prefer short verbs over managerial jargon. When a page-verified quote is brief and carries the main idea, put it on the slide *and* in the lesson.
Public captions: title · credit · licence · source link. **Never** `resource_uuid`, `forger_version`, or review tags in square brackets. **Geometrical background slides** (`analysis_opener`, `lab_opener`, `workshop_opener`, `outro`) — their caption **must** include the SVG file UUID (the content-hash suffix visible in the filename, e.g. `ct-pass-01-structure.svg#a1b2c3`) so a forger pass can trace which specific fractal was shown. See §"Golden rules (2026-09-14)" below.
**TTOD index gate:** every Tao-origin quote must be traceable in the unit
payload with its TTOD `id`, roman `number`, `form`, and lexicum `fields`.
These fields are an index for the forge and evaluator; do not turn them into a
student-facing editorial label or citation. A missing field fails cold review.

**Image backgrounds (lab / workshop / analysis_model):** when the live deck shows a flat diagram or empty `none` where a fashion/design still should carry the idea, set `background_kind: profield` and a real `media_slot_id`. Do not leave `lab_exercise` or `workshop_work` on `none`/`diagram` if an accepted unit asset exists.

## Golden rules (captured 2026-09-14 after live U1 teaching; quote rule revised 2026-09-15)

Five rules override any conflicting habit above and bind every subsequent unit's slideshow:

1. **Typography is a little bigger overall.** Base `.reveal` size is now `clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 38px)`; headings scale proportionally. Do **not** revert to the pre-2026-09-14 clamps just because a slide "looks empty." A row-8 teenager reading a projection must not squint — that is the acceptance test, not screenshot aesthetics.
2. **Write every slide as if for a 17-year-old high-school teenager (golden rule).** Short sentences. Concrete verbs. One idea per slide. No managerial abstractions (`stakeholder alignment`, `strategic ideation`), no untethered jargon. If a sentence would not survive being read aloud to a curious teenager, rewrite it before it ships. Keep the register the same across all six units.
3. **Quote hierarchy — Ahmes first; Tao invent when Ahmes has no brief match.** Every substantive slide (cover, analysis_model, masterclass, lab_exercise, workshop_work) should carry a brief, specific `quote:` that sharpens the sentence — not a paraphrase of the heading.
   - **Prefer page-verified vault extracts.** Resolve via `semantic-quote` against a real extraction database node with evaluator-safe status. Full provenance (coat, node_id, page_index, printed_page, verbatim) lives in a switch-gated Markdown comment in the **lesson** file. Student `content.json` carries the verbatim string + `quote_origin: page_verified` + `citation.label` (Chicago author-date) + `citation.href` (anchor into the lesson's References). **Never** write the corpus product name into `content.json` or public lesson HTML.
   - **If no brief page-verified match:** invent one line in the voice of **The Tao of Creativity** (CT/TC) and propose it into TTOD via `ttod-bridge` (never hand-edit `ttod.yml`). Set `quote_origin: tao_invented`, `citation.label: (Tao of Creativity)`, and `citation.href` to `{{ '/tao/#<chapter-id>' | relative_url }}` (monograph: `docs/tao/`). Invents are studio aphorisms, never disguised as scholarly quotation. Forge loop: [`TAO-OF-CREATIVITY-FORGE.mdc`](./TAO-OF-CREATIVITY-FORGE.mdc) + cascade [`TAO-OF-CREATIVITY/INDEX.md`](./TAO-OF-CREATIVITY/INDEX.md).
   - **Semantic tags (required whenever `quote` is set).** Attach DH-aligned metadata on the slide object (not rendered to students by default):
     - `semantic_tags.themes` — short controlled phrases (e.g. `idea-generation`, `lateral-thinking`, `authorship`)
     - `semantic_tags.cidoc` — CIDOC-CRM classes when useful (e.g. `crm:E33_Linguistic_Object`, `crm:E73_Information_Object`)
     - `semantic_tags.getty_aat` — Getty AAT-style labels when useful (e.g. `aphorisms`, `design (discipline)`)
     - `semantic_tags.dcterms` — Dublin Core when useful (`dcterms:subject`, `dcterms:type=Text`)
     - For Ahmes quotes also keep coat/node in the lesson's switch-gated comment (publication firewall).
4. **`(Author, Year)` is always a link.** Every author-date citation on a slide **and** in the lesson body must be an anchor into that lesson's `## References` section (`href: #ref-<surname>-<year>` on the slide's `citation.href`, `<a href="#ref-...">(Author Year)</a>` in the lesson Markdown). A bare parenthetical `(Author 2003)` with no link is a defect — the same rule already binds U1's `(Craft 2003, 43)`, apply it forward. Tao invents use the Tao label + link instead of a fake scholarly author-date.
5. **AI-declaration filiation** — authorship footer is Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD (`ruvebal@crea-comm.net`) only. Never append `(ECSIT / UEM)` (see `ct-unit-forge` §4b).

These rules are checked by cold review before a lesson's `status:` may move off `pilot`.

